     <div class="sect3">
+     <h4 id="pveceph_mute_health_check">
+      8.14.4. Mute a Health Check
+      <a class="headerlink" href="#pveceph_mute_health_check" title="Permalink to this heading">
+      </a>
+     </h4>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       Muting a health check keeps it visible but excludes it from the overall health
+status, making new problems easier to notice. Ceph continues evaluating the
+check. Use a duration so that a deferred warning returns automatically, for
+example after two weeks:
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="listingblock">
+      <div class="content">
+       <!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight
+by Lorenzo Bettini
+http://www.lorenzobettini.it
+http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
+       <pre><tt>ceph health mute <span style="color: #990000">&lt;</span>CHECK<span style="color: #990000">&gt;</span> 2w</tt></pre>
+      </div>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       In the web interface, expand the check under
+       <strong>
+        Datacenter → Ceph
+       </strong>
+       , click
+       <em>
+        Mute
+       </em>
+       , and set a duration. The check stays in the list, marked as muted; use
+       <em>
+        Unmute
+       </em>
+       in the same place to restore it earlier.
+      </p>
+     </div>
+     <div class="paragraph">
+      <p>
+       By default, a mute clears when more items become affected. Enable
+       <em>
+        Keep Mute
+       </em>
+       ,
+or add
+       <span class="monospaced">
+        --sticky
+       </span>
+       to the command, only if the check should stay muted in that
+case. This does not change the duration: a timed sticky mute still expires.
+      </p>
+     </div>
